# Statistical tables

## Total lolines in roots

|Treatment            | _CHISQ  |*p*-value   |
|:--------------------|:-------:|:---------:|
|Foliar clipping (F)  | 4.205   |**0.040** | 
|Root cutting (R)     | 1.041   |0.3074    |
|Root herbivory (H)   | 6.239   |**0.012** |
|F _CROSS R           | 1.054   |0.3046    |
|F _CROSS H           | 0.000   |0.9850    |
|R _CROSS H           | 2.191   |0.1388    |
|F _CROSS R _CROSS H  | 0.764   |0.3820    |

: _TABLE_LOLINES: Type III analysis of variance (ANOVA) results for the effects of foliar clipping (F), root cutting (R), root herbivory (H), and their interactions on total lolines. Each row presents a Type III Wald χ² test for the corresponding term after accounting for all other terms in the model. "_CROSS" denotes an interaction between treatments. Bold *p*-values indicate statistical significance (α = 0.05).

